      "writtenOn": "2017-07-31T14:28:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, I tried to count the number of times we hit line 6814 experimentally this morning using RTApp (EnergyModelWakeMigration Lisa test) on Hikey960. I observed the following:\n\n - 1248 find_best_target() calls hit line 6814 at least once\n - 249 find_best_target() calls hit line 6814 at least twice\n\nThis 1/5 ratio is probably because picking a good target_cpu in the first place prevents from assessing the others. So I think we should definitely not just save target_cpu before 6814 but also modify 6804 and 6808 significantly to remember the second best target_cpu as you suggested. Otherwise, we will be able to pick a sensible second target_cpu only if we are lucky enough to iterate over the CPUs in a favourable order.",
      "parentUuid": "7f1c344e_1e05abf9",
